// Day 26 - p50 and p99 latency, by endpoint.
//
// Question this answers: for each HTTP route the API serves, how fast are
// successful and unsuccessful requests, at the median and at the tail? p50 tells
// you the typical experience; p99 tells you what your slowest 1-in-100 requests
// look like, which is what a real latency complaint is usually about (the
// complainant is almost never a median request).
//
// `name` is Application Insights' pre-parsed "METHOD /route" operation name -
// grouping by it, not the raw URL, avoids splintering the same endpoint into one
// row per distinct id/query-string value.
requests
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| summarize
    RequestCount = count(),
    P50Ms = percentile(duration, 50),
    P99Ms = percentile(duration, 99)
    by EndpointName = name
| order by RequestCount desc
